# No dependency in this project needs to compile anything on install.
#
# better-sqlite3 ships prebuilt binaries (prebuilds/<platform>-<arch>.node,
# built against Node-API so they work across Node versions), but it also
# contains a binding.gyp - and npm's default behaviour for any package with a
# binding.gyp is to run `node-gyp rebuild`. On a machine without Visual Studio
# Build Tools that fails, which is what breaks `npm ci` here. The prebuilt
# binary is present either way, so skipping install scripts gives a working
# install without a C++ toolchain.
#
# Side effect worth knowing: this disables install scripts for *every*
# dependency. Today none of them need one. If a future dependency genuinely
# requires a build step, it will fail at runtime rather than at install time -
# remove this line then and install the build tools instead.
ignore-scripts=true
